]\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\arc-outline.md:27:[Omitted long matching line]\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\arc-outline.md:123:- **Target length**: Content-driven, no word target. **Depth band: standard-plus** — 6 points, but two of the book's nine cross-cutting themes originate here (namespaced-vs-cluster-scoped; labels/selectors as the universal join)\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\arc-outline.md:218:- **Notes**: Blocking gap G25 (Gateway API detail). **NetworkPolicy is taught once, here** — Ch 12 cross-bears in rather than duplicating. `ch10-zenith` is the named home of cross-cutting theme #3, \"the object exists but nothing happens without the component\"; name the pattern here so Ch 13 and Ch 17 can retrieve it by name.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\arc-outline.md:248:- **Notes**: Blocking gaps G5 (PSS/PSA, `securityContext`), G6 (4Cs), G7, G22 (supply chain), G23 (policy engines). **[B3]** `ch12-fig02` must be *derived* from `ch04-fig04`, not presented as a memorization table — this is the payoff for cross-cutting theme #2. Pair `ch12-zenith` with Ch 10's NetworkPolicy additive semantics: two systems, one rule, no deny.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\arc-outline.md:349:- **Retrieval targets**: **~100%** **[B3]** — the chapter is retrieval by definition. All nine cross-cutting themes are surfaced by name here, and every confusion pair from B1's trap inventory that survived to publication gets a discriminating question\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\arc-outline.md:350:- **Key concepts introduced**: None new. Reorganizes the book along the nine cross-cutting themes rather than along the four domains, so the reader sees the material a second time in a different shape\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\arc-outline.md:459:1. **Re-run B3 or accept the reconstruction.** Six of nine cross-cutting themes here are B5-reconstructed. They are defensible, but they are not B3's list.\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\retrieval-architecture.md:15:[Omitted long matching line]\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\section-skeleton.md:40:| §6 | Controllers and the Control Loop | **the control loop** — desired state, current state, reconciliation; the controller pattern. **Definition home for cross-cutting theme 1** |\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\section-skeleton.md:49:| §1 | You File a Declaration | declarative vs imperative; the object as an artifact of intent; `kubectl apply` semantics. **Definition home for cross-cutting theme 4** |\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\section-skeleton.md:51:| §3 | Where a Name Lives | namespaces; the four initial namespaces; **namespaced vs cluster-scoped**. **Definition home for cross-cutting theme 2** |\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\section-skeleton.md:53:| §5 | The Universal Join | labels; annotations; equality-based and set-based selectors. **Definition home for cross-cutting theme 5** |\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\section-skeleton.md:69:| §8 | What a Pod Is Owed | **requests vs limits**; QoS classes (Guaranteed, Burstable, BestEffort). **Definition home for cross-cutting theme 8** |\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\section-skeleton.md:193:| §7 | Numbers Nobody Collects by Default | the resource metrics pipeline; metrics-server; `kubectl top` and why it fails on a bare cluster — **retrieved by name as cross-cutting theme 3, defined at Ch 10 §3**; cluster log architecture and node-level agents. **Definition home for metrics-server** — Ch 17 §7 and Ch 18 §3 refer |\nC:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\book-outline\\section-skeleton.md:261:| §7 | Four Things That Scale | **the